# Governance artifacts are records, not shipped documentation.
#
# design/ holds TRDDs and the PRRD. Terminal TRDDs (column: complete / published /
# superseded / cancelled) are FROZEN by the TRDD rules — their bodies must not be
# edited after the transition that closed them, because they are the audit trail of
# what was decided and when. Linting a file that may not be edited produces findings
# that can never be cleared, which is the definition of a check that cannot pass: it
# blocks the publish gate forever and trains everyone to bypass the gate.
#
# The PRRD is written by prrd-edit.py, not by hand, so its layout is the tool's to
# decide and a hand-fix here would be reverted on the next rule edit anyway.
design/

# Regeneratable or private, never shipped.
reports/
reports_dev/
.trashcan/
node_modules/
